<http://data.silknow.org/object/cdd81858-b1ec-37a8-8aea-57a9dcf09fe7/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Outer trousers (ue no hakama) for a man, part of the formal dress of the Japanese Imperial Court, with long waist ties and two broad strips which loop front to back at crotch. White twill silk with wisteria roundels, with red lining which shows at the edges of the sides, hems, waist bands, ties and loops. Pairs of cords, threaded through and tied in places in elborate knots, decorate the long waist bands and there are laced double cords at the top of the side seams."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdd81858-b1ec-37a8-8aea-57a9dcf09fe7> .

