<http://data.silknow.org/object/cdd81858-b1ec-37a8-8aea-57a9dcf09fe7>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Outer trousers (ue no hakama) for a man, part of the formal dress of the Japanese Imperial Court, with long waist ties and two broad strips which loop front to back at crotch. White twill silk with wisteria roundels, with red lining which shows at the edges of the sides, hems, waist bands, ties and loops. Pairs of cords, threaded through and tied in places in elborate knots, decorate the long waist bands and there are laced double cords at the top of the side seams."@en , "The formal costume for male members of the Japanese court is known as ‘sokutai’ and consists of various layers of long upper garments, or hô, and two pairs of hakama, a type of lower garment variously described as full-cut trousers or a divided skirt. This is a pair of outer hakama, woven in white silk with roundels of wisteria. This wide garment is slightly pleated at the top, open at the sides, and ties around the waist with broad bands. The red silk lining is revealed at the side openings, hems, along the bands and on the two broad loops that conceal the opening at the crotch.  White, laced double cords reinforce the top of the side seams, and pairs of cords, elaborately knotted at intervals, decorate the long waist bands."@en , "Man's court outer trousers (ue no hakama) of white figured silk, Japan, 1800-1880"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/983620b0-7674-3072-8c12-99718eff6572> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/040270cb-8a60-312a-a2ba-5f7a81dd6153> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Outer trousers (ue no hakama) for a man, part of the formal dress of the Japanese Imperial Court, with long waist ties and two broad strips which loop front to back at crotch. White twill silk with wisteria roundels, with red lining which shows at the edges of the sides, hems, waist bands, ties and loops. Pairs of cords, threaded through and tied in places in elborate knots, decorate the long waist bands and there are laced double cords at the top of the side seams."@en , "Man's court outer trousers (ue no hakama) of white figured silk, Japan, 1800-1880"@en , "The formal costume for male members of the Japanese court is known as ‘sokutai’ and consists of various layers of long upper garments, or hô, and two pairs of hakama, a type of lower garment variously described as full-cut trousers or a divided skirt. This is a pair of outer hakama, woven in white silk with roundels of wisteria. This wide garment is slightly pleated at the top, open at the sides, and ties around the waist with broad bands. The red silk lining is revealed at the side openings, hems, along the bands and on the two broad loops that conceal the opening at the crotch.  White, laced double cords reinforce the top of the side seams, and pairs of cords, elaborately knotted at intervals, decorate the long waist bands."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdd81858-b1ec-37a8-8aea-57a9dcf09fe7/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/cdd81858-b1ec-37a8-8aea-57a9dcf09fe7/dimension/1> ;
